#order 0
#substr
#function
#reportsections

#rem First insert functions that will not be protected

#rem Insert some modules that need not be protected
#module
vorbisfile:
vorbisfilemt:

#function

#rem Determine which functions have to be fade protected.

#order 30
WinMain@16
CDKey

#rem Include also some functions, that do not need to be protected,
#rem but we think it can do no harm to protect them
#rem Note: any reference to DLL makes function protection impossible
#module

#function

#rem Functions that perform Fade protection should go here
#rem Such functions are protected by checksum
#rem Any tampering with them should result in crash
#rem Protect all InGameUI (this is where we draw fade messages)

#order 20

CheckFade
CRCCalculator
ProcessKeyPressed
InGameUI
RifleInaccuracy@Man

#rem Add also some functions that need not be protected
#rem to hide better what we are really doing.

AimWeapon@Man
Simulate@Man
TrackTargets@EntityAI
Think@AIUnit
Think@AIGroup

#rem CD Protection cannot be protected (self-modifying code)
#order 10

?CDP
?CDAPFN0506

#rem After CD Protection insert some functions that may but need not be protected
#rem to provide some space for checksum space padding to DWORD.

#order 11
GetWeaponDirection
AISubgroupContext


#rem Some functions are identical between several modules
#rem and linker replaces them with one common instance.
#rem This can cause ordering problems when when function is merged
#rem with library functions.
#rem We reset ordering preferences for such functions to 10000
#rem to avoid such conflicts.

#rem Put some unique functions before library functions, as they sometimes
#rem cannot be ordered and we need an end marker for the CRC region
#rem The function should call no DLL functions to prevent warning, as it
#rem can be partly included in the CRC region as well
#order 9999

GlanceRandomDirection@AIBrain

#order 10000
#module
LIBC:
LIBCMT:

#rem All other functions remain unprotected (order==10000)
